    <h1>What is Nitro cold brew coffee</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke. <time datetime="2020-07-21">July 21, 2020</time> (updated <time datetime="2020-08-03">August 3, 2020</time>).</p>

    <p>An introduction from the founder and CEO of Bona Fide, answering the basic question: what is nitro coffee?</p>

    <h2>What is nitro coffee?</h2>
    <p>Nitro coffee is cold brew coffee infused with nitrogen. It pours with a cascading look and a creamy, smooth texture, and is served cold from a tap.</p>

    <h2>Cold brew and coffee on tap</h2>
    <p>Cold brew is coffee steeped in cold water, and coffee on tap serves it straight from a keg. See <a href="/nitro-cold-brew/">nitro cold brew</a>, <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a> and <a href="/coffee-on-tap-is-the-future/">why coffee on tap is the future</a>.</p>
